## Change safety

Run before commit / `@ui-component-build complete`:

| Gate | Command | Fail when |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Touch scope | `bash scripts/touch-scope-verify.sh` | File outside `.work.ui/touch-scope` |
| Blast radius | `bash scripts/blast-radius-check.sh` | Cross-area diff ≥3 areas |
| Tests | `bash scripts/framework-verify.sh` | Non-zero exit |
| Gate check | `bash scripts/gate-verify.sh` | Done task with empty Notes |

**Declare scope first:** Copy `templates/work.ui/touch-scope.template` → `.work.ui/touch-scope`.

---

## Framework hard rules

- New skills **must** use `ui-` prefix; never `plan-master`, `code-implementation`, `session-control`, etc.
- Project artifacts from skills go to **adopter** `<repo-root>/.work.ui/` — not into `templates/` except template sources.
- Do not copy MOD concept ids into `concepts/`.
- Do not overwrite `.ai/` or adopter `.work/` from this framework (see Data loss below).

---

## Data loss & destructive operations

**Permission rule:** Explicit human approval is required for every action below. Approval applies **only to the current request (same message)** — it is never standing or permanent permission.

Unless the human operator explicitly requests it in the **same message**, agents MUST NOT:

| Action | Examples (non-exhaustive) |
|--------|---------------------------|
| **Git publish / rewrite** | `git commit`, `git push`, force-push, hard reset, `git clean -fd`, amend of published history |
| **Database destroy** | `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, wipe, reset, or bulk-delete of any database, schema, table, volume, or equivalent datastore |
| **Filesystem delete** | Delete files or directories (`rm`, project-tree wipe, emptying generated artifact trees) |
| **Overwrite protected trees** | Overwrite `.ai/`, adopter `.work/`, or replace an existing `.cursorrules` wholesale (merge only, or `confirm-overwrite-cursorrules` when named in the same message) |

Creating or editing files in declared task scope is allowed. Prefer reversible edits over delete or overwrite. When unsure, stop and ask.

---

## Protected Files

High-blast paths that require explicit same-message operator approval to modify, rename, or delete. Canonical list: `standards/PROTECTED_SURFACES.json` — covers `agent.os.framework.md` (framework source marker, content fixed, never deployed), `.cursorrules`, `hooks/`, `standards/`, and the verifier scripts (`framework-verify`, `touch-scope-verify`, `blast-radius-check`, `gate-verify`, `cursorrules-verify`).

---

## Git

- Commit/push only per **Data loss & destructive operations** above.
- No attribution ("Generated by", "Created by", dates, or agent signatures) in committed files.
- No `Co-authored-by:` trailers (mandatory). Enforced by hooks. Install: `bash scripts/install-git-hooks.sh`.
- Commit subject: `UIS-123: description` when ref known, else `type: description` (`feat`/`fix`/`refactor`/`docs`/`chore`).

---

## Templates (substance required)

When adding templates under `templates/work.ui/`, include enough default content that bootstrap produces usable HANDOFF_UI, NEXT_UI, and registries — mirror Agent OS `.ai/templates/work/` depth.

Canonical adoption guide: `docs/adoption/FROM_AGENT_OS.md`.
